model Rental_orders {
  id String @id @default(uuid())

  customerId String
  customer   Users  @relation(fields: [customerId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)

  startDate DateTime
  endDate   DateTime

  totalAmount Decimal @db.Decimal(10, 2)

  createdAt        DateTime           @default(now())
  updatedAt        DateTime           @updatedAt
  rentalOrderItems RentalOrderItems[]
  reviews          Reviews[]
}

// The thing is that according to the data model, how will it create an order? It will take the customer ID from the authentication request.user. It will take the start date and end date. The total amount will be calculated from the rental order items model. It will take the price from there, then how many items he got, and then it will take the start date and end date, calculate the days between them, and then do some math to calculate the total amount. 